  static const String _privacyEnglish = '''
PRIVACY POLICY — LEFFERION PRIME - MIZAN
Effective date: 16 August 2026

1. Scope and publisher. This Privacy Policy explains how the LEFFERION PRIME - MIZAN application (the “App”) handles information. The publisher and support contact are the developer identity and contact details displayed on the App’s current Google Play listing. Those listing details must be kept accurate before public release.

2. Core financial records. The App is designed so that the user’s people, debts, bills, subscriptions, rents, installments, expenses, income, payment history, notes, categories and related financial tracking records are stored locally on the user’s device unless the user deliberately exports, saves or shares them. The publisher does not need the contents of those records to provide ordinary local tracking functionality.

3. Exports and sharing. CSV backups and PDF reports are created at the user’s request. When the user chooses a destination or sharing application, the selected file is transferred to that destination under the receiving service’s own privacy terms. The user is responsible for protecting exported files because they may contain sensitive financial information.

4. Free-mode connectivity and advertising. The free version requires an internet connection. The App may perform small reachability requests to determine whether real internet access is available. These requests do not intentionally include the user’s financial ledger. As with ordinary internet communication, the endpoint and network providers can receive technical information such as IP address, time and basic request metadata. Free users may receive advertising through Google Mobile Ads. Where legally required, the App uses Google’s User Messaging Platform or another required consent mechanism before requesting personalized or otherwise regulated advertising and provides a privacy-options entry point when required.

5. Premium purchase information. Lifetime Premium is sold through Google Play as a one-time in-app product. The App receives Google Play purchase information and a purchase token needed to verify ownership and restore entitlement. For production verification, the purchase token is sent to the publisher’s monetization backend, which validates the purchase with Google Play. The backend stores a cryptographic hash or other minimized record needed for entitlement, fraud prevention, refund/revocation handling and support; it should not store raw payment-card information. Payment credentials are processed by Google Play, not by the App.

6. Promotions and device-abuse prevention. To enforce the rule that a promotion code may be used only once per eligible device, the App derives a pseudonymous device identifier from Android’s app-scoped device identifier and hashes it before transmission. A production promotion request is also intended to be protected by Google Play Integrity so the backend can reject unrecognized or materially tampered installations. The backend stores keyed cryptographic representations of the device and promotion identifiers, redemption time and temporary-Premium expiry. These records are retained for as long as needed to enforce the relevant promotion, prevent repeated redemption, resolve disputes and meet applicable legal obligations. If a promotion is permanently retired and the uniqueness record is no longer needed, it should be deleted or irreversibly anonymized within a reasonable operational period.

7. Purposes and legal bases. Information is processed only for purposes such as providing requested app functionality, verifying purchases, restoring entitlements, enforcing promotion limits, preventing fraud and abuse, maintaining security, complying with law, handling support, and serving advertising to free users. Where consent is legally required for advertising or similar processing, consent is requested before that processing. Other processing may rely on performance of a contract, legitimate interests such as security and fraud prevention, or another lawful basis available under applicable law.

8. Service providers and international processing. Google Play, Google Mobile Ads, Google Play Integrity, Cloudflare infrastructure and other processors necessary for the described functions may process technical data in countries other than the user’s own. Their processing is also governed by their own terms and privacy notices. The publisher should use appropriate contractual, organizational and technical safeguards where cross-border-transfer law requires them.

9. Retention. Local financial records remain on the device until the user deletes them, clears the App’s storage, uninstalls the App without preserving a backup, or otherwise removes them. Purchase-verification records are retained only as long as reasonably needed for entitlement, refund/revocation, fraud prevention, support, accounting or legal obligations. Advertising and consent records follow the applicable provider settings and legal retention requirements. No retention period should be longer than necessary for its stated purpose.

10. Security. The App uses measures intended to reduce unauthorized access, including local-storage validation, HTTPS for backend requests, cryptographic hashing of identifiers, server-side purchase verification and production integrity checks. No device, transmission or storage system can be guaranteed absolutely secure. Users should protect their device, Google account and exported files with appropriate security controls.

11. Choices and rights. Depending on location, users may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, or obtain a copy of personal data processed by the publisher, and may have the right to withdraw consent without affecting earlier lawful processing. Advertising privacy choices are available in the App when required. Requests concerning publisher-controlled backend data can be submitted using the developer contact shown on Google Play. Requests concerning Google-controlled payment or advertising data may also need to be directed to Google.

12. Children. The App is a personal financial-tracking utility and is not designed or marketed as a child-directed service. Users who are not legally able to enter the relevant agreements in their jurisdiction should use the App only with any consent or supervision required by local law.

13. Changes. This Policy may be updated when functionality, providers or law changes. Material changes should be presented in the App or through another reasonable notice method before or when they take effect where required.

14. Language. Localized versions are provided for accessibility. The English version is the controlling reference for interpretation to the maximum extent permitted by law. This language clause does not waive or reduce any mandatory right that local law gives the user.
''';

  static const String _termsEnglish = '''
TERMS OF USE — LEFFERION PRIME - MIZAN
Effective date: 16 August 2026

1. Agreement and eligibility. By using the App, the user agrees to these Terms and the Privacy Policy. If local law requires parental, guardian or other authorization, the user must obtain it before use. Mandatory legal rights that cannot lawfully be excluded remain unaffected.

2. Purpose of the App. MIZAN is a personal record-keeping and reminder tool for debts, bills, subscriptions, rents, installments, expenses, income, payments and related records. Calculations, reminders, dates, summaries and reports depend on information entered by the user and on device conditions. The App does not provide banking, investment, tax, accounting, legal, credit, debt-collection or other regulated professional advice. Users remain responsible for verifying amounts, due dates, contractual obligations, taxes, fees and decisions with the relevant institution or qualified professional.

3. Free and Premium access. Free access may require continuous internet connectivity, may display advertising, and does not include PDF report export. Premium access removes App-served advertising, permits offline use and enables PDF report export while the entitlement is valid. Temporary Premium may be granted through eligible rewarded advertising or promotions and expires automatically at the stated time. Lifetime Premium is a separate one-time Google Play entitlement with no recurring subscription charge and no preset expiration date, subject to valid ownership, refund/revocation rules, platform availability and these Terms.

4. Advertising. Free users may encounter full-screen advertising only at intended transition points and rewarded advertising when they deliberately request a reward opportunity. Advertising availability, content and targeting may be supplied by third parties such as Google. The publisher does not guarantee that an ad will always be available. Premium users are not intended to receive App-served ads while Premium is valid.

5. User data and backups. The user is responsible for the accuracy of records entered into the App and for maintaining backups appropriate to the importance of those records. Local data can be lost through device failure, factory reset, operating-system behavior, user deletion, storage corruption or other events. CSV exports should be stored securely. The publisher should not be treated as a bank, archival custodian or guaranteed backup provider.

6. Acceptable use. Users may not intentionally bypass Premium controls, advertising gates, purchase validation, promotion limits, Play Integrity checks or other security controls; forge purchase or promotion responses; automate abusive redemption attempts; interfere with the service or another user; distribute modified builds that misrepresent entitlement; introduce malware; or use the App in violation of applicable law. Security research conducted lawfully and responsibly should be reported through the developer contact rather than used to exploit users or the service.

7. Availability and changes. The publisher may maintain, fix, improve or change the App, supported operating-system versions, infrastructure, advertising providers and non-essential features. Reasonable efforts should be made not to remove a paid core entitlement without a legitimate reason. Internet services, Google Play, advertising inventory and third-party infrastructure can be unavailable outside the publisher’s control.

8. Intellectual property and license. Subject to these Terms, the user receives a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the App for lawful purposes. The App’s software, branding, original interface assets and other protected material remain with their respective rights holders. These Terms do not transfer ownership of the App to the user.

9. Disclaimer and liability. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the App is provided without a guarantee that every reminder, calculation, export, network check or third-party service will always be uninterrupted or error-free. The publisher is not responsible for losses caused by relying on unverified financial entries, missed external payment obligations, user-provided incorrect information, third-party outages or insecure handling of exported data. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability or remedies that applicable law does not permit to be excluded, including mandatory consumer rights.

10. Suspension and entitlement enforcement. The publisher may restrict server-backed promotional or purchase-verification functions when reasonably necessary to investigate fraud, abuse, tampering or legal requirements. A refunded, charged-back, cancelled, invalid or fraudulently obtained purchase may cease to confer Premium once the status can be reliably verified. Local financial records should not be deleted merely because Premium ends.

11. Governing rules and disputes. These Terms operate together with mandatory laws applicable to the user and the publisher. No clause is intended to force a consumer to give up a mandatory forum, remedy or protection that cannot legally be waived. Before formal proceedings, users are encouraged to contact the publisher through the Google Play developer contact so technical or purchase issues can be investigated.

12. Language and severability. Localized versions are provided for accessibility. The English version is the controlling reference to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law. If a clause is unenforceable, it should be limited or separated only to the extent necessary while the remaining clauses continue to operate.
''';

  static const String _purchaseEnglish = '''
PURCHASE TERMS — LIFETIME AND TEMPORARY PREMIUM
Effective date: 16 August 2026

1. Lifetime Premium product. Lifetime Premium is intended to be offered through Google Play as the one-time, non-consumable product “premium_lifetime”. It is not a subscription, does not renew automatically, and has no recurring subscription fee. The price and currency shown in the Google Play purchase sheet at checkout are the binding store price for that transaction, including any taxes or regional pricing applied by Google or applicable law. The commercial target may be approximately USD 5.00, but the App must display and rely on the current Google Play price rather than hard-coding a currency amount.

2. What Lifetime Premium unlocks. While valid, Lifetime Premium provides an ad-free App experience, offline App use and PDF report export. “Lifetime” means the entitlement has no preset time-based expiry; it does not promise that a particular device, operating system, third-party store or online infrastructure will exist forever. The publisher must not represent the product as a recurring subscription.

3. Automatic restore and account ownership. The App intentionally does not require a visible restore button. On supported Android installations, the App silently checks Google Play ownership when the store is reachable and listens for purchase updates. A verified prior purchase can restore the entitlement after reinstalling the App or moving to another compatible device when Google Play reports the same valid ownership. The user generally needs to use the Google account that owns the purchase. A locally cached verified entitlement may continue to permit Premium offline so that a previously verified purchaser is not forced online on every launch.

4. Verification and acknowledgement. Purchase tokens may be verified by the publisher’s backend against Google Play before permanent Premium is granted. Valid purchases are acknowledged as required by Google Play. Verification is used to prevent forged entitlements, replay attacks and unauthorized Premium activation. Raw payment-card details are not handled by the App.

5. Refunds, withdrawals and mandatory rights. Refund eligibility is governed by Google Play rules, applicable consumer law and any additional publisher obligations. Rules vary by country, purchase type and time since purchase. Nothing in these Purchase Terms removes a statutory cancellation, conformity, refund or other remedy that cannot legally be waived. If Google Play or another authorized process refunds, cancels, reverses or revokes the purchase, Premium access may be removed when the App or backend can reliably verify that ownership is no longer valid.

6. Temporary Premium from rewarded ads. A free user may be offered the opportunity to complete three eligible rewarded ads in the same reward day. After the third verified reward event, the App grants a 24-hour temporary Premium period. Rewarded-ad inventory is not guaranteed, the reward has no cash value, cannot be transferred, and is not a purchased subscription. Premium users do not need and should not see this reward control while Premium remains valid.

7. Promotion codes. ESMANUR is configured to grant seven days of temporary Premium and LEFFERION is configured to grant three days of temporary Premium, subject to server verification. Each of those codes may be redeemed at most once on an eligible device. The App may use a pseudonymous device identifier and Play Integrity to enforce this limit across uninstall/reinstall cycles. Promotion benefits have no cash value, are not transferable, and may be rejected when the device, installation, request integrity, code or prior-redemption status cannot be verified. Promotional periods may coexist with other temporary entitlement only according to the App’s stated extension rules; they do not convert into a refund entitlement.

8. Price changes and promotions. The publisher may change the price offered to future purchasers or introduce, modify or end promotions, subject to Google Play rules and applicable law. A later price change does not create a recurring charge and does not retroactively change a completed one-time purchase.

9. Purchase support. For delivery, restore or entitlement issues, the user should first verify that Google Play is using the account that owns the purchase and that the device is compatible. Support can be requested using the developer contact shown on the Google Play listing. Refund requests may also need to be submitted through Google Play according to the rules applicable to the user’s transaction and location.

10. Language. Localized explanations are provided for accessibility. The English version is the controlling reference for interpretation to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, without reducing mandatory local consumer rights.
''';

